{# The routes through here that have a page of their own.

   Anchor text, mostly. Until this block existed nothing on the site linked a
   route page except the footer's five, so 153 of the 158 were pages only the
   sitemap mentioned -- and a page nothing links to is a page nothing vouches
   for. These say the whole pair rather than just the far end: under a heading
   about Montreal, "Paris" is a weaker thing to read than "Paris to Montreal",
   and the pair is both what the page it opens is about and the phrase somebody
   types to look for it.

   Counted, not curated. RouteRepository ranks these by how often the pair has
   been searched and offers only pairs that can be flown nonstop, which is the
   rule the footer's five follow and the reason none of these is a 404.

   One direction per page, the direction the page is already about: a city page
   reads "Flights to Montreal" and lists the routes arriving, an airport page
   reads "Flights from Heathrow" and lists the ones leaving. Between the two,
   every route page is linked from somewhere. #}
<ul class="chips">
    {% for route in routes %}
        <li>
            <a class="chip chip--link" href="{{ route.url }}">
                <i class="fas fa-route chip__icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ route.from_name }} to {{ route.to_name }}
            </a>
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
